1://! The system-wide model registry: every configured provider's refresh
2://! status and every model a provider has listed, in a dedicated Cozo owner.
3://!
4://! A successful refresh replaces a provider's availability with exactly what
5://! it listed: new models are added, listed models are marked available, and
6://! models it no longer lists are kept but marked unavailable, so their first
7://! and last sighting survive. A failed refresh changes only the provider's
8://! status; its last good list stays. A provider removed from the
9://! configuration is marked `removed` and its models unavailable. Every
10://! refresh advances the registry revision. A model's Control Plane profile,
11://! recorded by `set_model_registry_profile`, lives in its own relation so a
12://! refresh replaces the provider's list without erasing that record. The
13://! model_registry plugin owns the typed contract; this module stores what
14://! it is given.
